nary present, no non-mutating auth probe). Proceeding; if codex-backed roles fail to start, treat as PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE and resolve.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Retained Run Notes (compaction-resilient essentials)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Epic 05 (derivation-inference): 6 stories, two-file tech-design shape, no prompt inserts. coverage.md confirms all 22 ACs / 15 TCs mapped.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Story 1 deletes CLI surface (src/cli/, src/cli.ts, bin, registry, 12 cli-process-*.test.ts suites, LHC_PROVIDER path); retirement.test.ts proves SDK-only API; must record Epic 04 parity deviation note (spawned inspect-health parity backfilled pre-Epic-05, surface deleted instead of carried).\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Story 2: createSdk provider XOR inference; ModelCall contract; 7-kind assignment validation; routing tests assert actual ModelCall input.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Story 3: adapter implements 7 DerivationProvider ops; 7 versioned prompts (smoothing-v1 settled, 6 pre-dial-in); goldens in test/goldens/prompts/; empty output = retryable empty_output; provenance config-stamped, never parsed from output; inference/ must not import domains/.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Story 4: FAILURE_CLASSIFICATION data table (rate_limit/timeout/network/empty_output/other retryable; auth/invalid_request terminal); safeCall containment + timeout; Epic 02 queue machinery unchanged.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Story 5: opt-in OpenRouter suite via LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY (LHC_OPENROUTER_MODEL optional); visible ran/not-ran accounting; Epic 04 lifecycle capstone under real adapter; keyed run recorded in completion notes (date, model, pass state); CI default zero network.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Story 6: boundary advance only on turn_end commit; whole-turn eviction oldest-first; peek-ahead stop in [target, target+1 turn); newest closed turn protected; config two-field 64k/32k max>target; floorTokens retired; Epic 03 test amendment ledger + red-manifest regeneration required. Independent of stories 2-5; POC refs 1cf2dc45, 6a9aa7a4, f12a850d.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Red/Green house pattern: red-verify = build+typecheck+lint+boundaries (no behavior tests). Targeted test slices: pnpm exec vitest run <files> from packages/lhc.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Acceptance per story: story-orchestrate accepted -> review final package -> run story gate (pnpm run verify) -> run verify-all -> baseline compare -> receipt -> commit -> advance.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"stderr\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"interrupted\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":false,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"isImage\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":false,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"noOutputExpected\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":false}}\\\\\\\\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/streams/003-implementor.stdout.log:510:{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"user\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"user\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"tool_use_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"toolu_01KcKEJme2U1ZLXNvySk5LPa\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"tool_result\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"export type DerivedFormState = \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"pending\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ready\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"failed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"blocked\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// Outcome on tool-activity summaries — mechanically stamped from the record\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// (isError/presence), never authored by the provider (AC-2.4).\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nexport type ToolOutcome = \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"succeeded\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"failed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"unknown\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// A composed form's record of a dependency that fell back during composition:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// names the source record and the form that was not ready (AC-3.2/3.3).\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nexport interface DependencyGap {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  subjectKind: SubjectKind;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  subjectId: string;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  form: FormKind;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// The read shape for one derived form's state row (DD-2, DD-3).\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nexport interface DerivedForm {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  subjectKind: SubjectKind;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  subjectId: string;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  form: FormKind;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  state: DerivedFormState;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  content?: string; // ready only\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  reason?: string; // failed | blocked\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  sourceVersion: number; // which version of the source this form derives from (DD-3)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  gaps?: DependencyGap[]; // composed forms; landed-with-fallback record\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  metadata?: DerivedFormMetadata; // mechanically stamped fields; never provider-authored\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  derivedAt?: string;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// One tool call's or result's receipt within a turn's composed account\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// (AC-3.8): the account text — what changed, as composed — plus the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// mechanically derived outcome. Derived from the composition input, never\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// from provider prose; stamped on the turn_rendering form so the chunk\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// summaries can read receipts machine-readably in turn order.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nexport interface ToolRunReceipt {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  messageId: string;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  activity: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"tool_call\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"tool_result\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  account: string;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  outcome: ToolOutcome;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// Mechanically stamped form metadata: tool outcomes (AC-2.4), the turn\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// rendering's tool-run receipts (AC-3.8), plus — at retry exhaustion — the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// final attempts/last-error copied from the work item before its row is\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// deleted (DD-1: the queue is not an audit table; durable outcome detail\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// lives here).\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nexport interface DerivedFormMetadata {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  outcome?: ToolOutcome;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  receipts?: ToolRunReceipt[];\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  attempts?: number;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  lastError?: string;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  // Epic 05 (DD-4): which provider/model/prompt produced the content —\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  // copied from the ProviderResult's config-known strings, never authored\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  // from model output. The deterministic provider never sets it.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  provenance?: ProviderProvenance;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// One row of an owner's repair report (Flow 4): the form's durable state\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// joined with the queue's mechanical detail for the live item still working\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// toward it, if any. The five operational situations read from this one row:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// never-attempted (pending, no queue), retrying (pending + queue with\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// attempts > 0), ready, failed (+ reason), blocked (+ reason) — no caller\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// ever needs a queue API.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nexport interface FormReportEntry extends DerivedForm {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  queue?: {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    status: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"queued\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"claimed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    attempts: number;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    lastError?: string;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    eligibleAt?: string;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  };\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// ── provider seam (DD-7) ─────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// Every operation returns content or a structured failure carrying\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// retryable-or-not; classification is the adapter's duty.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// Provenance: the three config-known assignment strings, stamped by the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// inference adapter (it alone knows the assignment) and copied by handlers\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// into form metadata (Epic 05 DD-4). Never derived from model output.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nexport interface ProviderProvenance {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  provider: string;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  model: string;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  prompt: string;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// ── derived_form read-back and the sanctioned state writer ───────\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ninterface RawFormRow {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  subject_kind: string;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  subject_id: string;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  form: string;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  state: string;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  content: string | null;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  reason: string | null;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  metadata: string | null;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  source_version: number | bigint;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  gaps: string | null;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  derived_at: string | null;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nexport function readDerivedForms(filePath: string): DerivedForm[] {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  const db = new DatabaseSync(filePath);\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  try {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    const rows = db\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      .prepare(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        `SELECT subject_kind, subject_id, form, state, content, reason, metadata,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                source_version, gaps, derived_at\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n         FROM derived_form ORDER BY subject_kind, subject_id, form`,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      )\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      .all() as unknown as RawFormRow[];\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    return rows.map((row) => {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      const record: DerivedForm = {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        subjectKind: row.subject_kind as SubjectKind,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        subjectId: row.subject_id,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        form: row.form as FormKind,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        state: row.state as DerivedFormState,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        sourceVersion: Number(row.source_version),\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      };\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      if (row.content !== null) record.content = row.content;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      if (row.reason !== null) record.reason = row.reason;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      if (row.metadata !== null) {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        record.metadata = JSON.parse(row.metadata) as { outcome?: ToolOutcome };\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      }\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      if (row.gaps !== null) record.gaps = JSON.parse(row.gaps) as DependencyGap[];\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      if (row.derived_at !== null) record.derivedAt = row.derived_at;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"is_error\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":false}]},\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"session_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"7428c05c-eec6-4310-9738-8828ad5ff5b2\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"uuid\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1a94c513-1123-40a3-a406-d725e039ace9\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"timestamp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"2026-06-12T23:24:11.494Z\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"tool_use_result\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"stdout\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"export type DerivedFormState = \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"pending\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ready\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"failed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"blocked\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// Outcome on tool-activity summaries — mechanically stamped from the record\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n// (isError/presence), never authored by the provider (AC-2.4).\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nexport type ToolOutcome = \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"succeeded\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"failed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"unknown\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n