for `@mariozechner/pi-ai` by removing Node-only side effects from default browser import paths ([#1814](https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/issues/1814)).\ntemp/lh-context-reference-copy/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/CHANGELOG.md:1489:- Tool definitions can customize the default system prompt with `promptSnippet` (`Available tools`) and `promptGuidelines` (`Guidelines`) while the tool is active ([docs/extensions.md](docs/extensions.md), [#1720](https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/issues/1720)).\ntemp/lh-context-reference-copy/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/CHANGELOG.md:1494:- Added optional `promptSnippet` to `ToolDefinition` for one-line entries in the default system prompt's `Available tools` section. Active extension tools appear there when registered and active ([#1237](https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/pull/1237) by [@semtexzv](https://github.com/semtexzv)).\ntemp/lh-context-reference-copy/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/CHANGELOG.md:1495:- Added optional `promptGuidelines` to `ToolDefinition` so active tools can append tool-specific bullets to the default system prompt `Guidelines` section ([#1720](https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/issues/1720)).\ntemp/lh-context-reference-copy/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/CHANGELOG.md:1508:- Changed the default image paste keybinding on Windows to `alt+v` to avoid `ctrl+v` conflicts with terminal paste behavior ([#1682](https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/pull/1682) by [@mrexodia](https://github.com/mrexodia)).\ntemp/lh-context-reference-copy/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/CHANGELOG.md:1573:- Added default skill auto-discovery for `.agents/skills` locations. Pi now discovers project skills from `.agents/skills` in `cwd` and ancestor directories (up to git repo root, or filesystem root when not in a repo), and global skills from `~/.agents/skills`, in addition to existing `.pi` skill paths.\ntemp/lh-context-reference-copy/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/CHANGELOG.md:1609:- Added `transport` setting (`\"sse\"`, `\"websocket\"`, `\"auto\"`) to `/settings` and `settings.json` for providers that support multiple transports (currently `openai-codex` via OpenAI Codex Responses).\ntemp/lh-context-reference-copy/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/CHANGELOG.md:1684:- Updated the Antigravity system instruction to a more compact version for Google Gemini CLI compatibility\ntemp/lh-context-reference-copy/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/CHANGELOG.md:1706:- Replaced Claude Opus 4.5 with Opus 4.6 as default model ([#1345](https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/pull/1345) by [@calvin-hpnet](https://github.com/calvin-hpnet))\ntemp/lh-context-reference-copy/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/CHANGELOG.md:1725:- Changed `models.json` provider `models` behavior from full replacement to merge-by-id with built-in models. Built-in models are now kept by default, and custom models upsert by `id`.\ntemp/lh-context-reference-copy/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/CHANGELOG.md:1739:- Fixed OpenAI Responses API requests to use `store: false` by default to avoid server-side history logging ([#1308](https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/issues/1308))\ntemp/lh-context-reference-copy/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/CHANGELOG.md:1772:- Fixed Bedrock default model ID from `us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-6-v1:0` to `us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-6-v1`\ntemp/lh-context-reference-copy/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/CHANGELOG.md:1780:- Updated default model for `anthropic` provider to `claude-opus-4-6`\ntemp/lh-context-reference-copy/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/CHANGELOG.md:1781:- Updated default model for `openai-codex` provider to `gpt-5.3-codex`\ntemp/lh-context-reference-copy/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/CHANGELOG.md:1782:- Updated default model for `amazon-bedrock` provider to `us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-6-v1:0`\ntemp/lh-context-reference-cop